## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design CKNE-driven fairness in shared cache systems, handle high churn scenarios, and ensure SLA compliance across thousands of tenants.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-QoS mapping: dynamic quota allocation, eviction policies, and prefetch budgets
- Real-time rebalancing cadence with latency guarantees
- Telemetry-driven fairness mechanisms and failure mode handling under multi-tenant load

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo CKNE-aware rebalancer (simplified)
function rebalance() {
  const cknes = collectCKNEScores(); // {tenant, ckne}
  cknes.forEach(t => {
    const quota = calculateQuota(t.ckne);
    const evictionRate = calculateEvictionRate(t.ckne);
    const prefetchBudget = calculatePrefetchBudget(t.ckne);
    updateTenantConfig(t.tenant, quota, evictionRate, prefetchBudget);
  });
}
